"""Credit Expert View: knowledge base.

Two kinds of content, kept apart on purpose:

1. SOURCED FACTS (FACTS): every fact carries one or more verbatim quotes from a public source
   (official statistics, government/BEE/TERI/SIDBI cluster studies, industry bodies, named news reports)
   and a link. engine/expert_sources.py re-fetches each source and checks every quote is still there.
   Rule enforced by tests: every number written in a fact's text must appear in one of its quotes
   (or in the source title/date). Nothing here was produced by an AI model.

2. PRACTICE GUIDANCE (FAMILIES): general credit practice for an industry type: facility structure,
   covenants, red flags, questions to the promoter, upgrade/downgrade triggers. It is labelled
   'Practice guidance' wherever it is shown, carries NO numbers (tests enforce this), and is never
   presented as local data.

Unknowns are not filled in: the page shows them grey ('not yet known').
"""

